  "findings": [],
  "summary": "ACCEPT. The exact base-to-candidate boundary was independently reviewed for correctness, security, deterministic identity/order, persistence and restart replay, migration compatibility, source containment, safe XML, authorization, runtime composition, Story 12.3 exclusions, test quality, and regression risk. QR-001 is closed: typed CodeGraph and Java proof preimages plus every stable manifest scalar and relational child are persisted and independently reconstructed, so stable tampering conflicts while excluded telemetry remains replay-invariant. QR2-001/T060 are closed: one Core comparator governs detector output, manifest tag 26, initial validation, durable reload, and replay; exact restart retries replay and deliberately noncanonical first commits conflict before mutation. QR3-001 is closed without weakening tests: the production detector keeps the canonical first 255 observations, adds one deterministic BoundExceeded Warning, canonically reorders the final retained set to exactly 256, and reports truthful complete totals with EvidenceTruncated=true; prepared Pre-Scan Results accept 256 while legacy v1 remains capped at 100; CreatePrepared validates and retains CatalogRuleIdentity so the canonical fingerprint preimage survives persistence. The focused QR3 detector and PostgreSQL commit/restart-Replay/external-reorder-Conflict run passed 6/6; classification plus PostgreSQL atomic and SQLite replay surroundings passed 41/41; the complete PreparedScanning suite passed 114/114 with one explicitly skipped pre-existing concurrency test when rerun outside the sandbox after the sandboxed WebApplicationFactory run hit Windows EventLog access denial. Web build passed with 0 errors and 9 existing package/reference warnings, and candidate git diff --check passed. The August Windows-host Vulgata/CodeGraph/Java/JDT-LS topology, CodeGraph 1.5.0 and JDT-LS/Java 21 stdio pins, PostgreSQL 17-only Docker requirement, no CodeGraphContext, and zero Story 12.3 Worker execution or Document generation remain intact. Residual limitation: this review relied on the checked-in real-host CodeGraph/JDT-LS qualification and did not rerun those comparatively expensive host tools; final pinned verification still owns that rerun. No Critical, High, Constitution MUST, authority, or regression-blocking finding remains."
